The upstream MIT text is in LICENSE, unchanged, and it governs both the
upstream source and the modifications described below.

Upstream version
  This repository vendors no upstream source. The Docker build clones the
  tag and commit pinned in UPSTREAM_REF and applies the patches in patches/.
  UPSTREAM_REF is the single copy of that version. The published image
  ghcr.io/zeroroot-ai/zitadel-login is tagged with the same upstream tag.

Modifications
  Copyright 2026 Zero Root AI. Zero Root AI modified the upstream
  application with three patches, all described in README.md:

  patches/0001-zeroroot-login-customizations.patch
    Wraps the brand logo in a link to NEXT_PUBLIC_LANDING_URL, gives the
    back button an optional href, and points the loginname page's back
    button at that landing origin. Three files. The diff renders exactly
    as upstream when NEXT_PUBLIC_LANDING_URL is unset.

  patches/0002-disable-image-optimization.patch
    Sets images.unoptimized in next.config.mjs, which removes the
    /_next/image route. Nothing in the app uses the image optimizer.

  patches/0003-redirect-on-vanished-auth-request.patch
    When the OIDC auth request or SAML request being completed no longer
    exists, sends the person to a fresh sign-in with a short message
    instead of showing "Unknown error occurred".

None of the three patches change credential verification. Password, MFA,
passkey, password reset, external identity providers and account selection
are upstream code, unchanged. Patch 0003 changes one terminal step after
verification already succeeded: what the app does when Zitadel reports that
the request record it is completing is gone.
